Package: trickle
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: application-independent cooperative bandwidth limiter
 trickle limits the network bandwidth used by arbitrary dynamically
 linked Linux programs through LD_PRELOAD. A small coordination daemon
 shares bandwidth between users and processes using weighted fair
 scheduling, per-user caps, process rules, and time-based schedules.
 .
 This is the modern neotrickle implementation. It keeps the familiar
 trickle and trickled command names but does not provide the classic
 command-line interface, /etc/trickled.conf format, or wire protocol.
 See /usr/share/doc/trickle/README.Debian and migration-classic.md.
